Licensing considerations for whoever finalizes this:
  - The editor links ESPER (GPL-3.0-or-later, first-party, its own repo) via
    FetchContent through include/internal/sct-esm, which constrains the
    editor's distributable license. The SKSE plugins under src/SKSE/ do not
    link it.
  - The editor links NIFFER (first-party, its own repo; published under
    GPL-3.0-or-later and also licensed by its copyright holder under other
    terms) via FetchContent through include/internal/sct-pipeline and
    sct-assets. Keeping NIFFER's CLA in force is what keeps the other-terms
    option open. The SKSE plugins under src/SKSE/ do not link it.
  - Bundled build tooling and dependencies carry their own licenses (e.g.
    HKX2E is MIT; CommonLibSSE, rapidyaml, etc. have their own terms).

Replace this file with the chosen license text before any public release.
